IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `theft-nouns`
IMPORT `theft-s15-21-fraud`
IMPORT `theft-s34-interpretation`

-- Theft Act 1968 ss 15 to 21: tests. Layer 1.
-- Expected values were written by hand from the text of the section named beside
-- them. Sections 15, 15A, 15B and 16 are blank in this text and have no tests.
-- Yes/no fields of a fixture are FALSE unless the fixture's name says otherwise.

§ `Fixtures`

§§ `Expected penalties`

GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected seven years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 7)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE
GIVETH A `Penalty stated by the Act`
`expected fourteen years on indictment` MEANS `Penalty stated by the Act` WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `the imprisonment ceiling` IS (`imprisonment for a term not exceeding a number of years` 14)
    `the fine ceiling` IS `the section states no fine`
    `a fine and imprisonment may be imposed together` IS FALSE

§§ `Gain and loss (s 34(2)(a))`

`gl neither` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS FALSE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS FALSE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS FALSE
`gl gain` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS TRUE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS TRUE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS FALSE
`gl loss` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS FALSE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS FALSE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS TRUE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS TRUE
`gl gain in something that is not money or property` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS TRUE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS FALSE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS FALSE
`gl loss in something that is not money or property` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS FALSE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS FALSE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS TRUE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS FALSE
`gl gain in property and loss in something else` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS TRUE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS TRUE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS TRUE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS FALSE
`gl gain in something else and loss in property` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS TRUE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS FALSE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS TRUE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS TRUE
`gl only the property fields` MEANS `Gain or loss facts` WITH
    `he had a view to gain for himself or another` IS FALSE
    `the gain he had in view was a gain in money or other property` IS TRUE
    `he intended to cause loss to another` IS FALSE
    `the loss he intended was a loss in money or other property` IS TRUE

§§ `False accounting (s 17)`


`fa nothing` MEANS `False accounting facts` WITH
    `dishonest in falsifying or using the accounts` IS FALSE
    `the gain or loss in view in falsifying or using the accounts` IS `gl neither`
    `the thing is an account, or a record or document made or required for an accounting purpose` IS FALSE
    `destroyed it` IS FALSE
    `defaced it` IS FALSE
    `concealed it` IS FALSE
    `falsified it` IS FALSE
    `made or concurred in making an entry in it which is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS FALSE
    `omitted or concurred in omitting a material particular from it` IS FALSE
    `in furnishing information for any purpose, produced or made use of it` IS FALSE
    `to his knowledge it is or may be misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS FALSE
`fa falsified for gain` MEANS `False accounting facts` WITH
